.\" Pretty terminal emulator manual page
.TH PRETTY 1 "2026-11-07" "Pretty 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pretty \- hardware accelerated, kitty-compatible terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pretty
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Pretty
is a GPU-accelerated terminal emulator implementing the kitty terminal protocol
and rendering through Vulkan or OpenGL ES 3.0+ using wgpu.  It supports kitty
graphics, the kitty keyboard protocol, OSC 8 hyperlinks, OSC 52 clipboard,
desktop notifications, true colour, ligatures, scrollback, split (tiling) panes,
and compositor blur under KDE/X11.
.PP
Metal and Direct3D are reserved interfaces and are not implemented; selecting
them reports a clear error rather than silently falling back.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-renderer " auto|vulkan|gles|metal|dx"
Select the rendering backend.  The environment variable
.B PRETTY_RENDERER
is consulted when the option is absent.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Use an alternate TOML configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-\-command " COMMAND"
Run COMMAND in the terminal instead of the login shell.
.TP
.BI \-\-font-size " PX"
Override the configured font size for this run (not persisted).
.TP
.BI \-\-opacity " VALUE"
Override background opacity for this run (not persisted).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-blur
Disable compositor blur for this run.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Start fullscreen.
.TP
.BI \-\-title " TITLE"
Set the initial window title.
.TP
.BI \-\-benchmark " FRAMES"
Continuously redraw a full terminal frame for FRAMES frames, print a benchmark
result and exit.  Useful for validating the 60 fps baseline.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-info
Print the selected backends, adapters, drivers and protocol level, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage information.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PRETTY_RENDERER
Default renderer when no command-line option is supplied.
.TP
.B PRETTY_CONFIG
Alternate configuration path.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Rust logging filter (for example \fBinfo\fR or \fBwgpu_hal=debug\fR).
.TP
.B TERM
Set to \fBpretty\fR for child processes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pretty/config.toml
User configuration, editable graphically with Ctrl+, or with an editor.
.TP
.I ~/.terminfo/p/pretty
Terminfo used when the system-wide entry is not installed.
.SH SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+,
Open or close the graphical settings panel.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+E / Ctrl+Shift+O
Split the focused pane to the right / below.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+W
Close the focused pane.
.TP
.B Alt+Arrow
Move focus to a neighbouring pane.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C / Ctrl+Shift+V
Copy the selection / paste the clipboard.
.TP
.B Shift+PageUp / Shift+PageDown
Scroll the history by one page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Q
Quit Pretty.
.SH FILES
The kitty compatibility matrix and test evidence are installed under
.I /usr/share/doc/pretty.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on normal exit; non-zero when the selected renderer or GPU cannot be
initialised or a mandatory package resource is missing.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Include the output of \fBpretty --print-info\fR, the GPU/driver, and the full
startup log with RUST_LOG=info.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kitty (1),
.BR xterm (1)
